  "durationSeconds": 62.979646,
  "caption": "There is a difference between being alone and feeling alone #deepthought #healing #growth",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "And suddenly, I'm in that phase again, where I don't really want to be around people. I don't want to go out, I don't want to explain myself, I don't want to answer a whole bunch of texts. I just want to be alone. And the funny thing is, I used to think that something was wrong with me, whenever I felt like this. I started wondering if I'm starting to become distant, if I was isolating myself, if I was losing interest in people, but I'm starting to understand myself a little more now. Sometimes I just need to disappear for a little while. Sometimes, I simply just need space to hear my own thoughts again. Life gets loud sometimes. Everybody wants something from you. Everybody has an opinion. Everybody needs your attention, and sometimes I just get tired of being accessible. So I pull back. I put my phone down to spend time with myself. Figure out what I'm feeling without somebody asking me to explain. And maybe I'm finally learning that solitude and loneliness aren't the same thing. There's a difference between being alone and feeling alone. Right now, I don't think I'm lonely. I think I just need myself. And I had to realize that's okay. Maybe sometimes, disappearing for a little while is how you find your way back to yourself.",
